Sharing a virtual journey is also an excellent way to reflect on a journey and share experiences with future students.
For example, every year Bennet School students in North Carolina design a website about their trip to State Capital, each year the site is updated, but old versions are kept online as a souvenir book.
Blogs can also help improve students’ writing. Even though students usually start their blogging experience with careless grammar and spelling, this usually changes with the existence of an audience.
As students are often the most critical audience, the blogger begins to strive to improve writing to avoid criticism.
