Goma is a tourist town in the Democratic Republic of Congo, towards the easter, near Rwanda.
In 2002, Goma was destroyed by the lava of the Nyiragongo volcano, which buried most of the streets of the city, especially in the center.
While Goma is considerably certain, it would be convenient to investigate before making any visits outside this city to assess the status of fighting that persists in North Kivu province.
The city is also the basis for climbing the Nyiragongo volcano and for some of the most economical mountain gorilla follow-ups in Africa.
