A curry is an herbal and spice dish, along with meat or vegetables.
Curry can be either "dry" or "wet" depending on the amount of liquid.
In the inland regions of northern India and Pakistan, yogurt is often used in curries; in southern India and other coastal regions of the subcontinent, coconut milk is commonly used.
With 17,000 islands to choose from, Indonesian food is a generic term to cover a wide variety of regional cuisines that are found throughout the country.
But, if used without any other qualifiers, the term usually means food originating in the central and eastern regions of the main island of Java.
Today, Javanese cuisine is easy to find everywhere in the archipelago and offers a wide variety of dishes seasoned in a simple way. The favorite flavors of Javanese are usually those of peanuts, chillies, sugar (especially Javanese coconut sugar) and various aromatic spices.
The stirrups are supports for the feet of the rider hanging from each side of the saddle.
They are more stable for the rider, but they may have safety problems because the rider's feet could become trapped.
If a rider throws himself from the horse but has a foot attached to the stirrup, it could be dragged if the horse runs away. In order to minimize this risk, several safety precautions can be taken.
To begin with, most riders wear riding boots with a heel and a thin sole and thin strength.
In addition, some saddles, in particular the English, have safety bars that allow strep leather to fall off the mount if a rider pulls it back when falling.
