Alpine sports, which include skiing and snowboarding, are popular sports that consist of sliding down slopes covered in downhill snow with skis or a surfboard tied to your feet.
Skiing is an important travel activity with many enthusiasts, often known as "ski bums," planning the entire holidays around skiing to a particular place.
The concept of skiing is very old ◗ there are cave paintings symbolizing skiers from before 5000 BC!
Alpine skiing as a sport dates back at least the 17th century, but it was in 1861 that Norwegians opened the first recreational skiing club in Australia.
Travelling with backpack on skis: this activity is also called rural skiing, ski tourism or ski hiking.
It is related, but it generally does not involve alpine skiing or mountaineering, the latter executed on rost terrain and that require much more rigid skis and boots.
Imagine a ski route as something similar to a hiking route.
