Europe is a relatively small continent but with many independent countries. Under normal circumstances, traveling between several countries would involve having to make many visa applications and passport checks.
The Schengen area, however, functions as a single country in this regard.
As long as you stay in this area, you can generally cross borders without having to pass passport control again.
In the same way, having a Schengen visa it is not necessary to apply for a visa for each of the Schengen countries separately, saving time, money and paperwork.
