Extreme weather condition is the general term for any dangerous meteorological phenomenon with the potential to cause damage, significant social disruptions, or loss of human lives.
Extreme weather conditions can occur around the world, and there are different classes that can depend on geography, topography and atmospheric conditions.
Strong winds, hail, excessive precipitation and uncontrolled fires are forms and effects of adverse climatic phenomena such as storms, tornadoes, water hoses and cyclones.
Severe regional and seasonal atmospheric phenomena include peaches, snowstorms and sandstorms.
It is strongly recommended that travelers are aware of any risk of adverse weather that affects their area as long as it could alter their travel plans.
