?zmir is Turkey's third-largest city, with a population of approximately 3.7 million inhabitants, the second largest port after that of Istanbul, and a very good transportation hub.
What was the ancient city of Izmir, is now a modern, developed and crowded shopping center, located around a huge bay and surrounded by mountains.
The large promenades, buildings with glass facades and modern shopping centers are dotted with traditional red roof tiles, the 18th century market and the old mosques and churches, although the city exhales an atmosphere more of Mediterranean Europe than of traditional Turkey.
