Christmas is one of the most important festivals of Christianity, and the birth of Jesus is celebrated there.
Also non-believers of Christian and non-Christian countries around the world have made their own many of the traditions surrounding the festival.
There is the tradition of spending Easter's Eve making the vigil somewhere in the open to watch the sun rise.
Of course, there are Christian theological explanations for this tradition, but it is very plausible that it is a pre-Christian spring and fertility ritual.
Most traditional churches often celebrate an Easter Vigil on Saturday night during the Easter weekend, and congregations usually start celebrations at midnight to celebrate the resurrection of Christ.
